    ($SATQ$b32eab9f$SATQ$, $SATQ$06a10eeb-f1d8-451b-a59e-6fa8b92f8fab$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$FSS$SATQ$, $SATQ$Form, Structure, and Sense$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Increased gender diversity is revitalizing the field of economics, according to Harvard&rsquo;s Claudia Goldin. The trailblazing accomplishments of Goldin, winner of the 2023 Nobel Prize in Economics for her work on women in the labor force, <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> to the value of scholars of diverse backgrounds in spurring research into previously unexplored, but vitally important, topics.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"011dc8ec-e59a-4edc-a949-db3fb085aaec","content":"<p>attests</p>"},{"id":"d1db1ed8-7b7f-4d14-bbeb-ad24925758f7","content":"<p>has attested</p>"},{"id":"9bd4a26b-a56b-4a3f-a38d-fbf4255f9489","content":"<p>is attesting</p>"},{"id":"f5d5c44e-67c9-40c2-9ba7-4a8fe89cd275","content":"<p>attest</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["f5d5c44e-67c9-40c2-9ba7-4a8fe89cd275"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The convention being tested is subject-verb agreement. The plural verb "attest" agrees in number with the plural subject "trailblazing accomplishments."</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the singular verb "attests" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the plural subject "trailblazing accomplishments." Choice B is incorrect because the singular verb "has attested" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the plural subject "trailblazing accomplishments." Choice C is incorrect because the singular verb "is attesting" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the plural subject "trailblazing accomplishments."</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, N